# CODEOWNERS — review routing and merge gating for Joshua.
#
# GitHub reads this file (not a YAML manifest) to decide who is auto-requested
# to review a pull request, and — once the `develop` ruleset enables "Require
# review from Code Owners" — whose approval is required to merge it.
#
# Two rules govern everything below:
#
#   1. LAST MATCHING PATTERN WINS, and it wins *completely*. Rules do not stack.
#      A rule on a subdirectory REPLACES the rule on its parent, so every child
#      entry must repeat every owner it wants — including @hsmoon5458.
#
#   2. LISTING SEVERAL OWNERS MEANS "ANY ONE OF THEM". Two owners on a line is
#      not a two-approval requirement; either one satisfies the gate. GitHub
#      cannot express "both of these people must approve" here.
#
# A trailing `/` matches the directory and everything under it. An owner must
# have write access to the repository, or GitHub silently ignores the entry.
#
# @hsmoon5458 is co-owner of every path, so a review is never blocked on a
# single person being unavailable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — catches the repository root files (README, MODULE.bazel, BUILD,
# VERSION, requirements*, docker-compose*, and the agent instruction files) and
# anything not matched by a rule below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                          @hsmoon5458

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Top-level directories.
#
# Every top-level directory is listed explicitly, even where the owner is the
# same as the `*` default above. The redundancy is deliberate: it makes an
# unowned top-level directory visible as a missing line, and gives each
# subsystem a place to hand ownership to someone else later.
#
# Enforced per-PR by hooks/codeowners_check.sh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.gemini/                  @hsmoon5458
/.github/                  @hsmoon5458
/ai/                       @hsmoon5458
/assets/                   @hsmoon5458
/config/                   @hsmoon5458
/docker/                   @donegjookim @hsmoon5458
/dockerfiles/              @donegjookim @hsmoon5458
# Docs are owned by every collaborator with write access, so a docs-only
# change is never blocked waiting on one person.
/docs/                     @heostar @piscesgh @donegjookim @hsmoon5458
/firmware/                 @heostar @hsmoon5458
/hooks/                    @hsmoon5458
